# Experimental Stellarium @VERSION@ Windows plug-in SDK

This SDK builds a minimal standalone C++ dynamic plug-in for the matching
official Stellarium Windows package. It is intentionally small and does not
define a stable, general-purpose Stellarium API.

It supports implementing `StelModule` and `StelPluginInterface`. The installed
headers are `core/StelModule.hpp`, `core/StelPluginInterface.hpp`, and their
`StelMainExport.hpp` dependency. Other declarations exported by
`stelMain.dll` are internal and are not implicitly supported.

## Compatibility

A plug-in built with this SDK is compatible only with this exact combination:

- Stellarium @VERSION@ from the same package build
- Windows @STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_ABI_ARCHITECTURE@
- @CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID@ toolset v@MSVC_TOOLSET_VERSION@
- Qt @QT_VERSION@
- @STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_ABI_CONFIGURATION@ configuration
- dynamic MSVC runtime (`/MD`)
- `StelPluginInterface` IID `org.stellarium.StelPluginInterface/2.0`

There is no ABI guarantee across Stellarium releases or separately rebuilt
packages. Rebuild the plug-in for every Stellarium package it supports. Do not
mix this SDK's DLL, import library, headers, or CMake files with another
Stellarium installation.

The source revision is `@STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_SDK_SOURCE_REVISION@` and the
package build ID is `@STELLARIUM_PLUGIN_SDK_BUILD_ID@`. Machine-readable build
information is in
`share/stellarium/plugin-sdk/StellariumPluginBuildInfo.json`.

## Build

Install the exact Qt version listed above and use the matching MSVC toolset.
A minimal `CMakeLists.txt` is:

```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.18)
if (POLICY CMP0091)
    cmake_policy(SET CMP0091 NEW)
endif()
project(MyPlugin LANGUAGES CXX)

set(CMAKE_AUTOMOC ON)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)
set(CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY MultiThreadedDLL)

find_package(Stellarium @VERSION@ EXACT CONFIG REQUIRED)

add_library(MyPlugin MODULE MyPlugin.cpp MyPlugin.hpp)
target_link_libraries(MyPlugin PRIVATE Stellarium::stelMain)
set_target_properties(MyPlugin PROPERTIES PREFIX "lib")
```

Configure a Release-only build and point `Stellarium_DIR` to this SDK's
`lib/cmake/Stellarium` directory. Link through `Stellarium::stelMain`; do not
manually define `STELMAIN_BUILD` or `STELMAIN_USE_DLL`.

## Install

For a plug-in ID `MyPlugin`, install the DLL as:

```text
%APPDATA%\Stellarium\modules\MyPlugin\libMyPlugin.dll
```

Run it only with the matching Stellarium package. The SDK copy of
`stelMain.dll` is for isolated link/load tests; do not put it in the plug-in
directory or overwrite a different Stellarium installation with it.

This SDK and `stelMain` are distributed under GNU GPL version 2 or later; see
`COPYING`. Qt and other dependencies remain subject to their own licenses.
